    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="25.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 25.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="25.2" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ gif aðor oððe mæg oððe fræmde þa ráde forsace, gylde þam cingce CXX scyll'.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="25.2" corresp="#wit-a">And gyf aðor oððe mæg oððe fremde þa rade forsace, gilde þam cyningce hundtwentig scillinge.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="25.2" corresp="#wit-q">Et si aliquis uel cognatus uel alienus illuc ire negauerit, soluat regi CXX solidos.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="25a.2" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ gyf aðor oððe mæg oððe fremde man ða ráde forsace, gylde ðam cynge hundtwelfti scill'.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And gif aðor oððe mæg oððe fræmde þa rade forsace, gylde þam cingce CXX scyllinga.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">And if anyone, either kinsman or stranger, refuses to ride [against him], he shall pay the king 120 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And if anyone, either his relative or a stranger, refuses to participate in the ride, he is to pay the king one hundred twenty shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und wenn entweder ein Verwandter [des Verbrechers] oder ein fremder (Mann B) diesen Zug verweigert, zahle er dem König 120 Schill.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And if either a kinsman [of the criminal] or a stranger (man, B) refuses this riding, let him pay the king 120 shillings.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="329"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_7-2">III Eg 7.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 7, 2</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_47-2">Leis Wl 47.2</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">A's ‘hundtwentig’ (= 120). Liebermann compares III Eg 7.2.</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">fræmde þa: fræmde man þa B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">cxx: hundtwelfti B</note>
      </div>
    </body>
